# wfg-log 1
# fixture edit-built — the audio side reporting itself, hand-written and hand-checked.
#
# Go.dot's rule is that state transitions are events and continuous readouts are
# not: the Edit coming into being is something a decision depends on, so it
# arrives as a logged command applied on the tick it was observed, exactly like a
# cue being created. This fixture is that rule, replayable.
#
# What it must prove is that the transition reproduces on a machine with no audio
# at all. Every record here replays against an engine holding no Tracktion, no
# device and no show — and if it did not, a log taken during a performance would
# be reproducible only on the machine that recorded it, which is not a log.
#
# Nothing here needs a document, deliberately, so it can run in the one-argument
# form beside the skeleton fixture.
A 0 0 engine audio.editBuilt s:"hosted" i:8 i:4 i:64
#
# Applying it again is applying it, not a conflict. The graph is fixed at show
# load (PRD §3.25) so in a real session this happens once — but a handler that
# stored what it was told and nothing else is what makes a log replayed twice,
# or replayed after a session that already ran, converge on the same state.
A 12 1 engine audio.editBuilt s:"hosted" i:8 i:4 i:64
#
# A show with no audio is a real show, and zero is a real answer. This is the
# case a range check written in a hurry refuses.
A 25 2 engine audio.editBuilt s:"" i:0 i:0 i:0
#
# A graph with minus four nodes is a message that got mangled on the way in.
# Refused rather than clamped: storing 0 would put a number nobody measured in
# front of every client reading the tree.
R 37 3 engine type-mismatch audio.editBuilt s:"hosted" i:8 i:4 i:-4
#
# The device is a string and the counts are integers, and the registry checks
# both before any handler sees them.
R 37 4 engine type-mismatch audio.editBuilt s:"hosted" s:"eight" i:4 i:64
#
# Reported by the audio side, but sendable by anyone — including a replay, which
# is the point. A command only the inside of the process could send would be a
# command this file could not contain.
A 50 5 udp:10.0.0.5:9000 audio.editBuilt s:"device" i:32 i:64 i:456
R 50 6 cli arity audio.editBuilt s:"hosted" i:8
